From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] applet: Draw every press of a chord's shortcut

A dbusmenu shortcut is a list of presses. The translator made a GTK
accelerator of the first and dropped the rest, so an item bound to a
chord, as VS Code's Open Folder... is to Ctrl+K Ctrl+O, showed "Ctrl+K"
alone: a shortcut that does something else, or nothing.

A GTK accelerator is one press, and GtkAccelLabel draws only what it
makes of one key and its modifiers. So the translator now writes a chord
as each press's accelerator with a space between them, "<Control>k
<Control>o", which GTK parses no key from: its accel label draws
nothing. The applet looks at each item GTK makes from the model as it's
put in a menu, and where the model's accelerator is a chord it draws the
presses after the label, as GTK writes each ("Ctrl+K Ctrl+O"), in a node
named "accelerator" so that a theme styles it as it styles an accel
label's, and right-aligned with the same padding, so that its text ends
where a one-press accelerator's does.

A one-press shortcut is the accelerator it was, and GTK draws it as
before. An empty shortcut, which the translator read past the end of, is
now an empty accelerator, which GTK draws as none.
---
 lib/menu-chords.vala                       | 163 +++++++++++++++++++++
 lib/menu-widget.vala                       |   2 +
 lib/meson.build                            |   1 +
 subprojects/appmenu-glib-translator/item.c |  47 +++---
 4 files changed, 194 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 lib/menu-chords.vala

